hadiths[213]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2523","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Verily"""
"2524","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\In Paradise there is a tree"""
"2525","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\There is not a tree in Paradise except that its tree is of gold"""
"2526","Abu Hurairah narrated:\We said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What is wrong with us that when we are with you our hearts are softened and we feel free of desire for this world"""
"2527","Ali narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Indeed in Paradise there are chambers whose outside can be seen from their inside"""
"2528","Abu Bakr bin 'Abdullah bin Qais narrated from his father that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\Indeed"""
"2529","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""In Paradise, there are a hundred levels, between every two levels is (the distance of) a hundred years"
"2530","Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Muddawiyah al-Tirmidhī narrated to us; al-Qāsim ibn al-Ḥakam al-ʿUranī narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Walīd al-Waṣṣāfī narrated to us, from ʿAṭiyyah, from Abū Saʿīd, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered his place of prayer and saw people who appeared to be grinning. He said: ""Know that if you frequently remembered the destroyer of pleasures, it would distract you from what I see. So increase the remembrance of the destroyer of pleasures: death. For no day passes upon the grave but it speaks, saying: 'I am the house of estrangement, I am the house of solitude, I am the house of dust, I am the house of worms.' When the believing servant is buried, the grave says to him: 'Welcome and greeting. You were the most beloved of those who walked on my surface to me. Now that you have been entrusted to me and have come to me, you will see how I treat you.' Then it expands for him as far as his sight reaches, and a door to Paradise is opened for him. And when the wicked or disbelieving servant is buried, the grave says to him: 'No welcome and no greeting. You were the most hated of those who walked on my surface to me. Now that you have been entrusted to me and have come to me, you will see how I treat you.' Then it closes in on him until his ribs interlock."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ interlaced his fingers, inserting some into the gaps of others, and said: ""And Allah appoints for him seventy dragons. If one of them were to breathe on the earth, nothing would grow on it as long as the world remains. They will bite him and scratch him until he is brought to the Reckoning."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""The grave is either a garden from the gardens of Paradise or a pit from the pits of Hell."" Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a gharīb ḥadīth; we do not know it except from this route."
"2531","Ubadah bin As-Samit narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\In Paradise"""
"2532","Abu Sa'eed narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\Indeed there are a hundred levels in Paradise"""
"2533","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:""Indeed, a woman from the wives of the people of Paradise, the whiteness of her shin is visible through seventy garments until her marrow is seen, and that is because Allah, he Exalted, says: As if they are corundum and Marjan. So, as for the corundum, it is a stone that if you were to enter a wire through it, then you polished its cloudiness away, you would surely be able to see it through it."" Another chain reports a similar narration"
"2534","Qutaybah narrated to us, Abu Ṣafwān narrated to us, from Yūnus, from al-Zuhrī, from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, who said:\n\n\We were tested alongside the Messenger of Allah"
"2535","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\Indeed the first batch to enter Paradise will appear like the moon of a night that is full. The second will appear like the color of the most beautiful (brightest) star in the sky. Each man among them shall have two wives"""
"2536","Anas narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\The believer shall be given in paradise such and such strength in intercourse .\"" it was said: \""O Messenger of Allah! And will he able to do that?\"" He said: \""He will be given the strength of a hundred"""
"2537","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\The first batch to enter Paradise will appear like the moon of a night that it is full"""
"2538","Dawud bin Amir bin Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas narrated from his father"
"2539","Abu Hurairah narrated from the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) that he said:\The people of Paradise are without body hair"""
"2540","Abu Sa'eed narrated concerning His (Allah's) statement \And couches"""
"2541","Asma' bint Abi Bakr narrated:\I heard the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) while mentioning the Lote-Tree of the Utmost Boundary"""
"2542","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) was asked:\What is Al-Kawthar?\"" He said: \""That is a river that Allah has given me\""- that is"""
"2543","Sulaiman bin Buraidah narrated from his father that a man asked the Prophet (ﷺ):\O Messenger of Allah"""
"2544","Abu Ayyub narrated that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (s.a.w) and said:\O Messenger of Allah"""
"2545","Mu'adh bin Jabal narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\The people of Paradise shall enter Paradise without body hair"""
"2546","Ibn Buraidah narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w)said:\The people of Paradise are a hundred and twenty rows"""
"2547","Hannād narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated to us; ʿUmar ibn Dharr narrated to us; Mujāhid narrated to us, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The people of the Suffah were the guests of the people of Islam. They had no family and no wealth. By Allah, besides Whom there is no deity, I used to press my liver to the ground from hunger, and I would tie a stone to my belly from hunger. One day I sat on the path they used to exit. Abū Bakr passed by me, so I asked him about a verse from the Book of Allah, only asking so that he would take me along. He passed by and did not do so. Then ʿUmar passed by me, and I asked him about a verse from the Book of Allah, only asking so that he would take me along. He passed by and did not do so. Then Abū al-Qāsim ﷺ passed by me. He smiled when he saw me and said: ""Abū Hurayrah."" I said: ""At your service, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Come along."" He went on, and I followed him. He entered his house, and I sought permission to enter, so he permitted me. He found a bowl of milk. He said: ""Where did this milk come from for you?"" It was said: ""So-and-so gifted it to us."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Abū Hurayrah."" I said: ""At your service."" He said: ""Go to the people of the Suffah and invite them."" They are the guests of the people of Islam; they have no family and no wealth. When charity came to him, he would send it to them and not take anything from it. When a gift came to him, he would send for them, partake of it, and share it with them. This distressed me, and I said: ""What is this bowl among the people of the Suffah when I am the one sent to them? He will order me to pass it around to them. What will I get from it? I had hoped to get enough from it to suffice me."" But there was no escape from obeying Allah and obeying His Messenger. So I went to them and invited them. When they entered and took their seats, he said: ""Abū Hurayrah, take the bowl and give it to them."" I took the bowl and began handing it to each man. He would drink until satisfied, then return it, and I would give it to the next, until I reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. All the people had drunk their fill. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the bowl, placed it on his hands, raised his head, smiled, and said: ""Abū Hurayrah, drink."" I drank. Then he said: ""Drink."" I kept drinking while he said: ""Drink,"" until I said: ""By Him Who sent you with the truth, I find no path for it."" He took the bowl, praised Allah, named Him, and drank. Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth."
"2548","Salim bin 'Abdullah narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\The breadth of the gate through which my Ummah shall enter Paradise is the distance that a good rider covers in three. (meaning three nights or three years and"""
"2549","Narrated Qutaybah, narrated Abū ʿAwānah, from Qatādah, from Abū Burdah ibn Abī Mūsā, from his father, who said: \O my son"
"2550","Ali narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Indeed in Paradise there is a market in which there is no buying nor selling- except for images of men and women. So whenever a man desires an image"""
"2551","Jarir bin 'Abdullah Al-Bajali narrated:\We were seated with the Prophet (s.a.w) when he looked towards the moon on the night of a full moon and said: \""Indeed you shall be placed before your Lord and you shall see Him as you see this moon. You will see Him without trouble. So if you are able to keep from becoming overwhelmed from prayer before the rising of the sun and before its setting"""
"2552","Suhaib narrated concerning His (Allah's) statement:For those who do good is the best (reward) and even more- the Prophet (s.a.w) said: \When the people of Paradise enter Paradise"""
"2553","# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Narrated by Hārithah ibn Muḍarrib (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nHe said: \We visited Khabbāb (may Allah be pleased with him) to enquire after his health"
"2554","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Do you crowd one another in order to see the moon on the night of a full moon? Do you crowd one another in order to see the sun?\"" They said: \""No.\"" He said: \""So verily"""
"2555","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""Indeed, Allah will say to the people of Paradise: 'O people of Paradise!' They will say: 'We respond to You, O our Lord,and we are at Your service.' Then He will say: 'Are you pleased?' They will say: 'Why should we not be pleased when You have given us what you have not given anyone from Your creation.' So He will say: 'I shall give you what is greater than that.' They will say: 'And what is greater than that?' He will say: 'I shall cover you in My Pleasure and I shall not become angry with you ever"
"2556","Narrated by Isḥāq ibn Mūsā al-Anṣārī, narrated by Muḥammad ibn Maʿn al-Madanī al-Ghifārī, narrated to me by my father, from Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said:\n\n\The grateful eater is equal in rank to the patient fasting person.\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This is a *ḥasan gharīb* hadith."""
"2557","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Allah will gather mankind on the Day of Resurrection on a single plane"""
"2558","Attiyah narrated from Abu Sa'eed in Marfu' form:\When it is the Day of Resurrection"""
"2559","Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Paradise is surrounded by hardships"""
"2560","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\When Allah created Paradise and the Fire"""
"2561","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Paradise and the Fire debated. Paradise said: 'The weak and the poor shall enter me"""
"2562","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\The least of the people of Paradise in position is the one with eighty thousand servants and seventy-two wives. He shall have a tent of pearl"""
"2563","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\The believer"""
"2564","Ali narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Indeed in Paradise there is a gathering for Al-Hur Al-'Ein wherein they rasie their voices. The creatures have not heard the likes of them.\"" [He said:] \""They say: 'We are the eternal ones"""
"2565","# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Hannād narrated to us:** Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Ḥawshab, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ghanm, from Abū Dharr (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said:\n\n> Allāh, the Most High, says: **\O My servants"
"2566","[Abdullah] Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Three shall be on dunes of musk\"" - it seems to me that he said:- \""on the Day of Resurrection. The first and the last of peoples shall envy them: A man who calls to the five [prayers] every day and night; a man who leads a group of people and they are pleased with him"""
"2567","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated a Marfu' narration:\There are three whom Allah"""
"2568","Abu Dharr narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:\There are three whom Allah loves and three whom Allah hates. As for those whom Allah loves: Then a man who came to a people and asked them by Allah"""
"2569","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\The Euphrates shall soon uncover a treasure of gold"""
"2570","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said similar to it"
"2571","Qutaybah narrated to us, Ibn Luha'iyyah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn 'Amr al-Mu'afiri, from Abu 'Abd ar-Rahman al-Hubuli, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Whoever remains silent shall be saved.\"" Abu 'Isa said: This is a gharib hadith; we know it only from the narration of Ibn Luha'iyyah. And Abu 'Abd ar-Rahman al-Hubuli is 'Abdullah ibn Yazid."""
"2572","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Whoever asks Allah (s.w.t) Paradise three times"""
"2573","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Hell will be brought forth on that Day (of Resurrection) having seventy thousand bridles"""
"2574","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Some of the Fire (in the shape of a long neck) will come out of the Fire on the Day of judgment. It will have two eyes which can see"""
"2575","Al-Hasan said:\While he was on the pulpit – the pulpit of Al-Basrah – `Utbah bin Ghazwain narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said: “Indeed a giant rock can be thrown from the brink of Hell and it will continue to fall into it for seventy years without reaching the bottom of it.”.He said: “`Umar used to say:'Increase in your remembrance of the Fire"""
"2576","Abu Sa'eed narrated that the Prophet SAW said:\As-Saud is a mountain in the Fire"""
"2577","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\Indeed a disbeliever's skin will be forty-two forearm lengths thick"""
"2578","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\The molar teeth of the disbeliever on the Day of Judgment will be like Uhud (mountain)"""
"2579","Abu Hurairah narrated a Marfu' narration:\The molar teeth of the disbeliever will be like Uhud (mountain)"""
"2580","Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:'Indeed the disbeliever's tongue will be stretched a Farsakh or two Farsakh"
"2581","Abu Sa'eed narrated regarding His (Allah's) statement:Kal Muhl"
"2582","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:Indeed Hamim will be poured over their heads. The Hamim will penetrate until it finds its way to his insides. Then whatever is inside him will fall out until it pours over his feet while it melts away. Then he will be reformed to how he was"
"2583","Abu Umamah narrated regarding His (Allah's) statement:\He will be given water of Sadid to drink"""
"2584","# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Narrated by Hanzalah al-Usayyidī** (may Allāh be pleased with him), who was among the scribes of the Prophet ﷺ:\n\nHe passed by Abū Bakr (may Allāh be pleased with him) while he was weeping. Abū Bakr said, \What is the matter with you"
"2585","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) recited this Ayah:Have the Taqwa of Allah as His due"
"2586","Abu Ad-Darda' narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\The inhabitants of the Fire will suffer from a hunger equal to the punishment they experience"""
"2587","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\And therein they will grimace in displace lips. -He will be grilled by the Fire until his upper lip is folded up reaching the middle of his head"""
"2588","Abdullah bin 'Amr bin Al-'As narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\If a pellet like this one"""
"2589","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\This Fire of yours"""
"2590","Abu Sa'eed narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\This fire of yours is one part from seventy parts of the fire of Hell"""
"2591","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\The Fire was kindled for one thousand years until it reddened"""
"2592","Abu Hurairah narrated:that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said: \The Fire complained to its Lord. It said: 'Some parts of me consume other parts.' So He allowed it to take two breaths: one during the winter"""
"2593","Narrated by Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, narrated by al-Layth, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said:\n\n\Indeed"
"2594","Anas said that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\Allah will say: 'Remove from the Fire whoever remembered Me one day"""
"2595","Ibn Masud narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\I know the last of the people of the Fire to depart from it. A man will exit it crawling"""
"2596","Abu Dharr narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\ I know the last of the people of the Fire to depart from the Fire and the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise. A man will be brought forth and He (s.a.w) will say: 'Ask about his small sins and hide his large sins.' So it will be said to him: 'Did you do this and that on such and such a day"""
"2597","Jabir narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\ Some of the people of Tawhid will be punished in the Fire until they are coals. Then the Mercy (of Allah) will reach them"""
"2598","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Whoever had the weight of a speck of faith in his heart will depart from the Fire.\"" Abu Sa'eed said: \""Whoever has doubt then let him recite: Indeed Allah does not deal unjustly with even the weight of a speck"""
"2599","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Indeed two men among those who entered the Fire will be screaming violently. So the Lord"""
"2600","Imran bin Husain narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:'A group from my Ummah will depart from the Fire through my intercession"
"2601","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\I have not seen the likes of the Fire in which the one who runs from it sleeps"""
"2602","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger Of Allah (s.a.w) said:\I looked into Paradise and I saw that the most of its people were the poor; and I looked into the Fire and I saw that most of its people were women"""
"2603","Imran bin Husain narrated that the Messenger Of Allah (s.a.w) said:\ I looked into the Fire and I saw that most of its people are women"""
"2604","An-Numan bin Bashir narrated that the Messenger Of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Indeed the person among the inhabitants of the Fire punished least [on the Day of Judgment] is a man who has two coals beneath his feet"""
"2605","Harithah bin Wahb Al-Khuzai narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Should I not inform you about the people of Paradise: They are every humble and weak person"""
"2606","Narrated Abu Hurairah:narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I have been ordered to fight the people until they say La Ilaha Illallah\"""""
"2607","Narrated Abu Hurairah:said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) died and Abu Bakr became the Khalifah after him"""
"2608","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I have been ordered to fight the people until they bear witness to La Ilaha Illallah"""
"2609","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Islam is based upon five: the testimony of La Ilaha Illallah"""
"2610","Narrated Abdullah bin Buraidah from Yahya bin Ya'mur who said:\The first person to speak about Al-Qadar was Ma'bad Al-Juhani.\"" He said: \""Humaid bin Abdur-Rahman Al-Himyari and I went out until we reached Al-Madinah"""
"2611","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\A delegation of Abdul-Qais came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: 'We are a tribe from Rabi'ah"""
"2612","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed among the believers with the most complete faith is the one who is the best in conduct"""
"2613","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivered a Khtubah in which he exhorted them"
"2614","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Faith has seventy-some odd doors"""
"2615","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by a man and he was chastising his brother about modesty"
"2616","Narrated Mu'adh bin Jabal:\I accompanied the Prophet (ﷺ) on a journey. One day I was near him while we were moving so I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Inform me about an action by which I will be admitted into Paradise"""
"2617","Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \If you see a man who comes to the Masjid then bear witness to his faith.\"" Because Allah"""
"2618","Narrated Jabir:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Between disbelief and faith is abandoning the Salat"""
"2619","Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Ḥabīb ibn Abī al-ʿAshrīn narrated to us; al-Awzāʿī narrated to us; Ḥassān ibn ʿAṭiyyah narrated to us, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that he met Abū Hurayrah. Abū Hurayrah said: ""I ask Allah to gather me and you in the market of Paradise."" Saʿīd said: ""Is there a market in it?"" He said: ""Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed me: 'When the people of Paradise enter it, they will settle therein according to the merit of their deeds. Then permission will be granted for the duration of a Friday of the days of this world. They will visit their Lord, and His Throne will be presented to them, and He will manifest Himself to them in a meadow of the meadows of Paradise. Pulpits of light, pearls, rubies, chrysolite, gold, and silver will be placed for them. The lowest of them—and there is no lowly one among them—will sit on mounds of musk and camphor. They will not see that the people of the chairs have a better sitting place than them.'"" Abū Hurayrah said: ""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Do you dispute in seeing the sun and the moon on the night of the full moon?' We said: 'No.' He said: 'Likewise, you will not dispute in seeing your Lord.' Not a man will remain in that gathering but Allah will converse with him privately, until He says to a man among them: 'O so-and-so, son of so-and-so, do you remember the day you said such-and-such?' He will remind him of some of his treacheries in the world. He will say: 'O Lord, did You not forgive me?' He will say: 'Yes, by the vastness of My forgiveness you have reached this station of yours.' While they are in that state, a cloud will overshadow them from above and rain down upon them a perfume the like of whose fragrance they have never smelled. Their Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will say: 'Rise to what I have prepared for you of honor. Take whatever you desire.' He said: 'We will come to a market surrounded by the angels, in which there is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has not occurred to any heart. What we desire will be carried to us; nothing is bought or sold there. In that market, the people of Paradise will meet one another. A man of high station will come and meet one lower than him—and there is no lowly one among them. He will be awestruck by what he sees on him of garments. His conversation will not end before he imagines something better than it on himself. That is because no one should grieve there.' Then we will return to our dwellings. Our wives will receive us and say: 'Welcome and greeting. You have come with a beauty better than that with which you left us.' We will say: 'We sat today with our Lord, the Compeller, and it is fitting for us to return with the like of what we returned with.'"" Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a gharīb ḥadīth; we do not know it except from this route. And Suwayd ibn ʿAmr narrated something of this ḥadīth from al-Awzāʿī."
"2620","Narrated Jabir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Between a slave of Allah and disbelief is abandoning the Salat"""
"2621","Narrated Abdullah bin Buraidah narrated from his father:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The covenant between us and them is the Salat"""
"2622","Narrated Abdullah bin Shaqiq Al-'Uqayli:The Companions of Muhammad (ﷺ) didn't consider leaving anything to be disblief except for the Salat"
"2623","Narrated Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib:that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Whoever is pleased with Allah as (his) Lord"""
"2624","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There are three things for which whomever has them"""
"2625","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The adulterer is not a believer while he is committing adultery"""
"2626","Narrated Ali bin Abu Talib:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever is penalized (for a crime) then his punishment has been hastened for him in the world"""
"2627","Qutaybah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Allah will gather the people on the Day of Resurrection on a single plain. Then the Lord of the Worlds will look down upon them and say: 'Let every person follow what they used to worship.' The cross will be manifested for the worshipper of the cross, images for the worshipper of images, and fire for the worshipper of fire. They will follow what they used to worship. The Muslims will remain. Then the Lord of the Worlds will look down upon them and say: 'Will you not follow the people?' They will say: 'We seek refuge in Allah from You. We seek refuge in Allah from You. Allah is our Lord. This is our place until we see our Lord.' He will command them and strengthen them. Then He will veil Himself, then appear again and say: 'Will you not follow the people?' They will say: 'We seek refuge in Allah from You. We seek refuge in Allah from You. Allah is our Lord, and this is our place until we see our Lord.' He will command them and strengthen them."" They said: ""Will we see Him, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""Are you harmed in seeing the moon on the night of the full moon?"" They said: ""No, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Then you will not be harmed in seeing Him at that hour."" Then He will veil Himself, then appear, then make Himself known to them, then say: ""I am your Lord, so follow Me."" The Muslims will stand, and the Sirāṭ will be laid down. They will cross it like the swiftest horses and mounts. Their cry on it will be: ""Salām, salām (Safety, safety)."" The people of the Fire will remain. A group will be thrown into it, then it will be asked: ""Are you full?"" It will say: ""Is there any more?"" Another group will be thrown in, and it will be asked: ""Are you full?"" It will say: ""Is there any more?"" Until they are packed into it, the Most Merciful will place His Foot in it, and it will close up, and it will say: ""Qaṭ, qaṭ (Enough, enough)."" When Allah admits the people of Paradise into Paradise and the people of the Fire into the Fire, death will be brought in the form of a ram. It will be stood upon the wall between the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire. Then it will be said: ""O people of Paradise."" They will look up in fear. Then it will be said: ""O people of the Fire."" They will look up in hope, hoping for intercession. Then it will be said to the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire: ""Do you know this?"" They will say: ""Yes, we know it. This is death which was entrusted with us."" Then it will be laid down and slaughtered upon the wall between Paradise and the Fire. Then it will be said: ""O people of Paradise, eternity with no death. O people of the Fire, eternity with no death."" Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth. — And there have been many narrations from the Prophet ﷺ like this, mentioning the vision of the Lord, the mention of the Foot, and similar things. The position of the people of knowledge among the Imams—like Sufyān al-Thawrī, Mālik ibn Anas, Ibn al-Mubārak, Ibn ʿUyaynah, Wakīʿ, and others—is that they narrated these things and said: ""These ḥadīths are narrated, and we believe in them, and it is not said 'how'."" This is the position chosen by the people of ḥadīth: that these things be narrated as they came, believed in, not interpreted, not imagined, and not asked ""how."" This is the position of the people of knowledge which they chose and followed. And the meaning of his saying in the ḥadīth: ""Then He makes Himself known to them"" means: He manifests Himself to them."
"2628","Narrated Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari:that the Prophet (ﷺ) was asked: \Which of the Muslims is most virtuous?\"" He said: \""The one from (the harm of) whose tongue and hand (other) Muslims are safe"""
"2629","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed Islam began as something strange and it will return to being strange as it began. So Tuba is for the strangers"""
"2630","Narrated Kathir bin 'Abdullah bin 'Amr bin 'Awf bin Zaid bin Milhah narrated from his father"
"2631","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The sign of a hypocrite is that whenever he speaks he lies"""
"2632","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: There are four things that whoever has them"
"2633","Narrated Zaid bin Arqam:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whenever a man makes a promise and he intends to fulfill it"""
"2634","Narrated Ibn Mas'ud:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A Muslim's fighting his brother is disbelief"""
"2635","Narrated Ibn Mas'ud:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Verbally abusing a Muslim is disobedience and fighting him is disbelief"""
"2636","Narrated Ad-Dhahak:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \It is not for a slave (of Allah) to vow about something he does not possess"""
"2637","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever says to his brother 'disbeliever' then it will have settled upon one of them.\"" Sahih"""
"2638","Narrated by Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, who both said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, who said: I heard Rib'i ibn Hirash narrating from Zayd ibn Thabit, who attributed it to Abu Dharr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said:\n\n\There are three whom Allah loves"
"2639","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr bin Al-'As:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed Allah will distinguish a man from my Ummah before all of creation on the Day of Judgement. Ninety-nine scrolls will be laid out for him"""
"2640","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The Jews split into seventy-one sects"""
"2641","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \What befell the children of Isra'il will befall my Ummah"""
"2642","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed Allah"""
"2643","Narrated Mu'adh bin Jabal:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do you know what Allah's right upon His slaves is?\"" I said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He said: \""His right upon them is that they worship Him alone and do not associate any partners with Him.\"" He said: \""And do you know what their right over Allah is if they do that?\"" I said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He said: \""That He will not punish them"""
"2644","Narrated Abu Dharr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Jibril came to me and gave me glad tidings"""
"2645","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \For whomever Allah wants good"""
"2646","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever takes a path upon which to obtain knowledge"""
"2647","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever goes out seeking knowledge"""
"2648","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Sakhbarah:narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever seeks knowledge"""
"2649","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever is asked about some knowledge that he knows"""
"2650","Narrated Abu Harun [Al-'Abdi]:\We went to Abu Sa'eed and he said: 'Welcome with the exhortation of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). Indeed the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Surely"""
"2651","Narrated Abu Harun [Al-'Abdi]:from Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Men will come to you from the direction of the east to learn. So when they come to you then exhort them to good.\"" He said: \""When Abu Sa'eed saw us he would say: 'Welcome with the exhortation of the Messenger of Allah"""
"2652","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr bin Al-'As:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed Allah does not take away knowledge by removing it from the people"""
"2653","Narrated Jubair bin Nufair:from Abu Ad-Darda who said: \We were with the Prophet (ﷺ) when he raised his sight to the sky"""
"2654","Narrated Ibn Ka'b bin Malik:from his father that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: \Whoever seeks knowledge to contend with the scholars"""
"2655","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever learns knowledge for other than (the sake of) Allah"""
"2656","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Aban bin 'Uthman:from his father who said: \Zaid bin Thabit left to go to Marwan during the middle of the day. We said: 'He did not send for him [during] this hour except to ask him about something.' So we got up to ask him"""
"2657","Narrated Simak bin Hard:\I heard 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrating from his father who said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'May Allah gladden a man who hears something from us"""
"2658","Narrated 'Abdul-Malik bin 'Umair:from 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud that he narrated from his father"
"2659","Narrated 'Abdullah [bin Mas'ud]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever lies upon me"""
"2660","Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not lie upon me"""
"2661","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever lies upon me\"" - I think he said - \""purposely"""
"2662","Narrated Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever narrates a Hadith from me which he knows is a lie"""
"2663","# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Narrated by Anas رضي الله عنه:**\n\nMahmūd ibn Ghaylān narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Shuʿbah and Hishām narrated from Qatādah, from Anas رضي الله عنه, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.\n\nHishām reported the wording: **\He will be taken out of the Fire.\""**\n\nAnd Shuʿbah reported the wording: **\""Take out of the Fire whoever said *Lā ilāha illā Allāh* (There is no god but Allah) and had in his heart the weight of a barley grain of goodness. Take out of the Fire whoever said *Lā ilāha illā Allāh* and had in his heart the weight of a wheat grain of goodness. Take out of the Fire whoever said *Lā ilāha illā Allāh* and had in his heart the weight of an atom of goodness.\""**\n\nAnd Shuʿbah said: **\""The weight of a *dhurrah*\""** (with light pronunciation"
"2664","Narrated Al-Miqdam bin Ma'dikarib:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Lo! Soon a Hadith from me will be conveyed to a man"""
"2665","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:\We sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for writing but he did not permit us"""
"2666","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\There was a man among the Ansar who would sit with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"2667","Narrated Abu Hurairah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave an address. So he mentioned a story in the Hadith"
"2668","Narrated Hammam bin Munabbih:that the heard Abu Hurairah say: \None of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) narrated more Ahadith from him than me"""
"2669","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Convey from me"""
"2670","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) to get a mount"""
"2671","Narrated Abu Mas'ud Al-Badri:that a man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) looking for a mount"
"2672","Narrated Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Intercede"""
"2673","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \No soul is wrongfully taken except that some of the burden of its blood is upon the son of Adam"""
"2674","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever calls to guidance"""
"2675","Narrated Ibn Jarir bin 'Abdullah:from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever starts a good tradition which is followed"""
"2676","Narrated Al-'Irbad bin Sariyah:\One day after the morning Salat"""
"2677","Narrated Narrated Kathir bin 'Abdullah [and he is Ibn 'Amr bin 'Awf Al-Musani]:narrated from his father"
"2678","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: 'O my son! If you are capable of (waking up in) the morning and (ending) the evening"""
"2679","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Leave me with what I left you. When I narrated a Hadith to you"""
"2680","Narrated Abu Salih reported a narration from Abu Hurairah:\It shall soon be that people are beating the livers of camels (meaning that they are hastening and traveling upon them) seeking knowledge. But they will not find anyone more knowledgeable than a scholar of Al-Madinah"""
"2681","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The Faqih is harder on Ash-Shaitan than a thousand worshipers"""
"2682","Narrated Qais bin Kathir:\A man from Al-Madinah came to Abu Ad-Darda when he was in Dimashq. So he said: 'What brings you O my nephew?' He replied: 'A Hadith reached me which you have narrated from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).' He said: 'You did not come for some need?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Did you come for trade?' He said: 'No"""
"2683","Narrated Abu 'Abdullah, Huraib ibn Mis'ar al-Azdi al-Tirmidhi, narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) addressed the people and admonished them, then said: \O assembly of women"
"2684","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Two things will not be together in a hypocrite: Good manners"""
"2685","Narrated Abu Umamah Al-Bahili:\Two men were mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). One of them a worshiper"""
"2686","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The believer will never be satisfied with the good he hears"""
"2687","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The wise statement is the lost property of the believer"""
"2688","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! You will not enter Paradise until you believe"""
"2689","Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:\A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'As-Salamu 'Alaykum (Peace be upon you).'\"" [He said:] \""So the Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Ten.' Then another came and he said: 'As-Salamu 'Alaykum Wa Rahmatullah (Peace be upon you"""
"2690","Narrated Abu Sa'eed:\Abu Musa sought permission to enter upon 'Umar. He said: 'As-Salamu 'Alaykum (Peace be upon you). May I enter?' 'Umar said: 'Once.' Then he was silent for some time. Then he said: 'As-Salamu 'Alaykum (Peace be upon you). May I enter?' 'Umar said: Twice.' Then he was silent for some time. Then he said: 'As-salamu 'Alaykum (Peace be upon you). May I enter?' 'Umar said: 'Three times.' Then he (Abu Musa) left. 'Umar said to the gate-keeper: 'What did he do?' He replied: 'He left.\"" He said: 'Bring him to me.' So when he came"""
"2691","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that Uman bin Al-Khattab said: \I sought permission (to enter) from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) three times"""
"2692","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\A man enter the Masjid and performed Salat while the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was sitting at the back of the Masjid. Then he came to greet him"""
"2693","Narrated Abu Salamah:that 'Aishah narrated to him that he Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to her: \Indeeed Jibril has sent Salam to you.\"" She said: \""And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His Blessings"""
"2694","Narrated Abu Umamah:\They said: 'O Messenger of Allah! When two men meet"""
"2695","# Hadith Translation\n\n**Narrated by Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nHe said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n> *\The adulterer does not commit adultery while being a believer; the thief does not steal while being a believer. However"
"2696","Narrated Sayyar:\I was walking with Thabit Al-Bunani. He passed by some boys"""
"2697","Narrated Asma bint Yazid:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed through the Masjid one day"
"2698","Narrated Anas:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: 'O my little son! When you enter upon your family then give the Salam"""
"2699","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The Salam is before talking.\"" With this chain it has been reported that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Do not invite anyone to the food until the Salam is given"""
"2700","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not precede the Jews and the Christians with the Salam. And if one of you meets them in the path"""
"2701","Narrated 'Aishah:that a group of Jews entered upon the Prophet (ﷺ) and they said: \As-Samu 'Alaik (death be upon you).\"" So the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Wa 'Alaik (And upon you).\"" So 'Aishah said: \""I said: '[Rather] upon you be death and the curse.'\"" So the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""O 'Aishah! Indeed Allah loves gentleness in every matter.\"" 'Aishah said: \""Did you not hear what they said?\"" He said: \""And I replied: 'And upon you"""
"2702","Narrated Usamah bin Zaid:that the Prophet (ﷺ) passed by a gathering in which the Muslims and the Jews were mixed"
"2703","Narrated Al-Hasan:from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The rider gives the Salam to the walking person"""
"2704","Narrated Hammam bin Munabbih:from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The young one gives the Salam to the elder"""
"2705","Narrated Fadalah bin 'Ubaid:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The horseman gives Salam to the walking person"""
"2706","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you arrives at the gathering"""
"2707","Narrated Abu Dharr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever lifts the curtain so that his sight enters the house before he was given permission"""
"2708","Qutaybah narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn ʿAjlān, from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān, from Ibn Muḥayrīz, from al-Ṣunābiḥī, from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, that he said: I entered upon him while he was dying. I wept. He said: ""Gently. Why do you weep? By Allah, if I am martyred, I will testify for you. If I am granted intercession, I will intercede for you. If I am able, I will benefit you."" Then he said: ""By Allah, there is no ḥadīth I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that contains good for you except I narrated it to you, except one ḥadīth, and I will narrate it to you today, as my soul is being taken. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever testifies that there is no deity but Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah, Allah forbids the Fire for him.'"" And in this chapter there are narrations from Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, ʿUthmān, ʿAlī, Ṭalḥah, Jābir, Ibn ʿUmar, and Zayd ibn Khālid. I heard Ibn Abī ʿUmar say: I heard Ibn ʿUyaynah say: Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān was trustworthy, reliable in ḥadīth. Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ gharīb ḥadīth from this route. Al-Ṣunābiḥī is ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUsaylah, Abū ʿAbd Allāh. And it has been narrated from al-Zuhrī that he was asked about the Prophet's ﷺ saying: ""Whoever says 'Lā ilāha illā Allāh' enters Paradise."" He said: ""This was only at the beginning of Islam, before the obligations, commands, and prohibitions were revealed."" Abū ʿĪsā said: The interpretation of this ḥadīth according to some people of knowledge is that the people of Tawḥīd will enter Paradise, and even if they are punished in the Fire for their sins, they will not abide therein eternally. And it has been narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, Abū Dharr, ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, Ibn ʿAbbās, Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, and Anas ibn Mālik from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: ""A people will come out of the Fire from the people of Tawḥīd and enter Paradise."" Thus it was narrated from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī, and more than one of the Tābiʿīn. And it has been narrated from more than one route from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the interpretation of this verse: (Perhaps those who disbelieved will wish they had been Muslims.) They said: When the people of Tawḥīd are brought out of the Fire and admitted into Paradise, those who disbelieved will wish they had been Muslims."
"2709","Narrated Sahl bin Sa'd As-Sa'idi:that a man peeked in on the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"2710","Narrated 'Amr bin Abi Sufyan:that 'Amr bin 'Abdullah bin Safwan informed him"
"2711","Narrated Jabir:\I sought permission to enter upon the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding a debt my father owed"""
"2712","Narrated Jabir:that the Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited them from returning to the women from a journey during the night"
"2713","Narrated Jabir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you writes something"""
"2714","Narrated Zaid bin Thabit:\I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while there was a scribe in front of him"""
"2715","Narrated Zaid bin Thabit:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered me to learn some statements from writings of the Jews for him"""
"2716","It was narrated to us by Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, who said: Abu Usamah narrated to us from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever takes a path seeking knowledge"
"2717","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that Abu Sufyan bin Harb informed him that Hiraql had sent for him while he was with a party of the Quraish"
"2718","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\When the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) wanted to write to the foreigners"""
"2719","Narrated Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad:\Two of my companions and I went and presented ourselves to the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ)"""
"2720","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that a man gave the Salam to the Prophet (ﷺ) while he was urinating"
"2721","# Hadith Translation\n\n## Arabic Text\n\nحَدَّثَنَا قُتَيْبَةُ، حَدَّثَنَا نُوحُ بْنُ قَيْسٍ، عَنْ أَبِي هَارُونَ الْعَبْدِيِّ، عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم قَالَ: \يَأْتِيكُمْ رِجَالٌ مِنْ قِبَلِ الْمَشْرِقِ يَتَعَلَّمُونَ فَإِذَا جَاءُوكُمْ فَاسْتَوْصُوا بِهِمْ خَيْرًا\"". قَالَ فَكَانَ أَبُو سَعِيدٍ إِذَا رَآنَا قَالَ مَرْحَبًا بِوَصِيَّةِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم. قَالَ هَذَا حَدِيثٌ لاَ نَعْرِفُهُ إِلاَّ مِنْ حَدِيثِ أَبِي هَارُونَ عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ.\n\n---\n\n## English Translation\n\nQutaybah narrated to us: Nuḥ ibn Qays narrated to us"
"2722","Narrated Abu Ghifar Al-Muthanna bin Sa'eed At-Ta'i:from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaimi from Jabir bin Sulaim who said: \I went to the Prophet (ﷺ) and I said: ''Alaikas-Salam (upon you be peace)' so he replied: 'Do not say \""'Alaikas-Salam\"" rather say As-Salamu Alaik.'\"" And he mentioned the story in its entirety"""
"2723","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would give the Salam he would do so three times"""
"2724","Narrated Abu Waqid Al-Laithi:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was sitting in the Masjid and the people were with him when three people came. Two of them came near the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and one went away. When the two stopped at the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) the said the Salam. One of them saw an opening in the circle so he sat there. As for the other one"""
"2725","# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Narrated by ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with both of them):**\n\nThe Prophet ﷺ said:\n\n> *\Whoever acquires knowledge for other than the sake of Allāh"
"2726","# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Narrated by Zayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nMahmoud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Abu Dawud informed us, Shu'bah informed us, 'Umar ibn Sulayman — from the descendants of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) — said: I heard 'Abdur-Rahman ibn Aban ibn 'Uthman narrating from his father, who said:\n\nZayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) came out from the presence of Marwan at midday. We said: \He would not have summoned him at this hour except to ask him about something.\"" So we stood and asked him"
"2727","Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \No two Muslims meet each other and shake hands"""
"2728","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that a man said: \O Messenger of Allah! When a man among us meets his brother or his friend should he bow to him?\"" He said: \""No.\"" The man continued: \""Should he embrace him and kiss him?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Should he take his hand and shake it?\"" He said: \""Yes"""
"2729","Narrated Qatadah:that he asked Anas bin Malik: \Did the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) use to shake each other's hand?\"" He said"""
"2730","Narrated Ibn Mas'ud:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \taking hold of the hand is from the completeness of the greeting"""
"2731","Narrated Abu Umamah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \From the complete of visiting the ill is that one of you place his hand on his forehead\"" - or he said - \""on his hand"""
"2732","Narrated 'Aishah:\Zaid bin Harithah arrived in Al-Madinah while the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was in his house. So he went and knocked at the door"""
"2733","Narrated Safwan bin Assal:\A Jew said to his companion: 'Accompany us to this Prophet.' So his companion said: 'Do not say: \""Prophet\"". For if he hears you (say that) then he will be very happy.' So they went to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to question him about nine clear signs. So he said to them: 'Do not associate anything with Allah"""
"2734","Narrated Umm Hani:\I went to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) during the Year of the Conquest"""
"2735","Narrated by Abd ibn Humayd and others, they said: Narrated to us Musa ibn Mas'ud, Abu..."
